Well, if we pick out the part that we think give us the most leverage.

125
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:48,550
It is the message of domain driven design.

126
00:08:48,550 --> 00:08:51,350
That a conceptual idea of what you are building is really essential.

127
00:08:51,350 --> 00:08:56,389
A application or system is not just a lot of code that happens to work.

128
00:08:56,389 --> 00:09:01,750
It's kind of like encapsulate and encode a certain set of ideas and how they work together.

129
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,990
So if you work on a finance system,

130
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:10,711
you should know what is an account in this kind of context as opposed from a transaction. which is something else.

131
00:09:10,711 --> 00:09:15,430
And they might in different solutions get together.

132
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:19,430
and have a little bit different meanings and different boundaries between them.

133
00:09:19,430 --> 00:09:21,269
But for this precise application we're building,

134
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:26,310
we need to have a sharp understanding of what we mean with the different things.

135
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:31,509
And that kind of deep understanding which eliminates a lot of misconceptions.

136
00:09:31,509 --> 00:09:38,470
and thus bugs is what we built the security upon.

