00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:16,310
So a domain object is most likely a concept that's native in that particular domain, right?

269
00:19:16,310 --> 00:19:21,350
I mean, if you talk about hospitality, then of course room number is very common.

270
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:24,950
If you're at a hotel and you say, "Hey, put this on my room and things like that."

271
00:19:24,950 --> 00:19:26,870
That's a concept that needs to be expressed in that domain.

272
00:19:26,870 --> 00:19:32,789
So a domain object is something that's very familiar in that context.

273
00:19:32,789 --> 00:19:35,029
I think it might be valuable also to point out.

274
00:19:35,029 --> 00:19:44,789
that we in modeling often see these domain objects coming out in two main flavors modeling wise.

275
00:19:44,789 --> 00:19:51,990
The most usual that people tend to be familiar with from object orientation basic 101 at universities.

276
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:55,110
and stuff like that are of course the entities.

277
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:57,669
It's something that concept that models something.

278
00:19:57,669 --> 00:20:04,710
which has got a lifespan and an identity that can be changed.

279
00:20:04,710 --> 00:20:06,710
So a stay at an hotel is something that might be prolonged.

280
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:11,669
It might have a tab associated with it which can grow.

281
00:20:11,669 --> 00:20:17,669
A person might be something that who can change their names.

282
00:20:17,669 --> 00:20:22,870
and grow older or change their relationships and states in different ways.

283
00:20:22,870 --> 00:20:26,789
The other big modeling tool is of course the value object.

284
00:20:26,789 --> 00:20:29,590
Which models a specific aspect of something.

285
00:20:29,590 --> 00:20:37,909
Like a color red or the number four or the duration of 24 hours.

286
00:20:37,919 --> 00:20:42,470
So it's a little bit more like writing something down on piece of paper.

287
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:47,190
and then you can be able to share it but you will not change it.

288
00:20:47,190 --> 00:20:53,350
A duration of 24 hours cannot be 25 hours because then it's another duration.

289
00:20:53,350 --> 00:20:57,110
So those two tools are very fruitful to keep apart.

290
00:20:57,120 --> 00:21:05,909
So want to make sure I understand correctly when you're talking about value objects generally they are immutable. Would that be a correct term to use?

